WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.650
More than a century ago, a boy named Shlomo Keha
grew up in the mountains of northern Yemen.

2
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:24.000
As a boy, he shared a book with three other
children. Years later in Aden, his own pupils
would sit around him.

3
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.820
In the study house in northern Yemen, books were
scarce.

4
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.420
“There were four of us children to one book.”

5
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.010
“And this way we could read the book…”

6
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:39.570
From the front or the back, from the right or the
left.

7
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.450
“We could read it.”

8
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.060
Shlomo was very small when he lost his father.

9
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:53.515
“When my mother died, I was perhaps fifteen.”

10
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.120
With both parents gone, Shlomo went to live with
his father’s sister, Badra.

11
00:00:57.185 --> 00:00:58.885
Work, too, was part of Shlomo’s childhood.

12
00:00:59.015 --> 00:01:01.195
“We worked as blacksmiths.”

13
00:01:01.325 --> 00:01:04.975
In the workshop they shaped iron, learning where
to place each hammer blow.

14
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.410
At nineteen, as he remembered it, he left the
mountains.

15
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:14.280
Shlomo set off on foot, leaving the stone houses
of the mountains behind.

16
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.040
“On donkeys.”

17
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.750
“It took us about two weeks.”

18
00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.830
“From place to place. We walked by day and slept
at night.”

19
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.850
From the mountains around Saada, the caravan
headed south.

20
00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.780
Shlomo counted the journey in days of walking. At
the end lay the port of Aden.

21
00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.300
In Aden, the boy who had shared a book now had
pupils of his own.

22
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:45.970
“I had children there, and I taught them.”

23
00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.230
“How old are you? I told them twenty-five.”

24
00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.990
He remembered being twenty at the time.

25
00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:56.440
“In the end they approved my aliyah.”

26
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.930
After about a year of teaching and waiting, it
was time to sail.

27
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.290
“From Aden we went by ship.”

28
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:10.750
Until now the journey was measured in footsteps.
From here the sea would carry him.

29
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:17.150
The ship sailed north through the Red Sea to the
Suez Canal.

30
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.390
“We stayed in Port Said for one day.”

31
00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:31.250
“From there they sent us a car from the Land of
Israel.”

32
00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:40.730
Beyond the canal, the road carried them east, all
the way to Tel Aviv.

33
00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:47.410
In Tel Aviv, Shlomo found a bed at the
immigrants’ hostel.

34
00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:51.640
In 1938, Yona Nakash and Shlomo Keha married.

35
00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:56.360
Yona was 17–18 and Shlomo was 30–31.

36
00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:02.020
Four years later, in 1942, Yona and Shlomo posed
with their family.

37
00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:07.400
Shlomo is 35 and Yona is 20–21.

38
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.060
Ruti is 2–3 and Elisheva is under one year old.
